WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.520
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:05.120
Before we start new work, it helps to clean up.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.160
In this lesson, you will learn to clear the console, and to remove old

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.480
values from the environment, one at a time or many at once.

5
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.000
A clean workspace is a calm workspace.

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.681
This is our new session.

7
00:00:20.681 --> 00:00:24.955
On the right, the environment still holds the values from last time.

8
00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:28.160
In the console, we see our old results too.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.524
First, the console.

10
00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:34.023
I write a note:

11
00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:36.272
to remove history from the console.

12
00:00:36.272 --> 00:00:38.520
The shortcut is Control and L.

13
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.162
Careful here:

14
00:00:52.162 --> 00:00:57.496
I typed Control L as code and ran it. R says: object not found.

15
00:00:57.496 --> 00:01:00.545
That is because Control L is not code.

16
00:01:00.545 --> 00:01:02.450
It is a keyboard shortcut.

17
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.260
Just click in the console, and press Control and L.

18
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.037
See?

19
00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:08.922
The console is clean now.

20
00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:11.560
The script and the environment are untouched.

21
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.605
Next, the environment.

22
00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:16.213
I write a note:

23
00:01:16.213 --> 00:01:20.231
to remove a data or value from the Global Environment.

24
00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:22.240
The function is called remove.

25
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.020
Inside the brackets, I write the name of the value. Remove age.

26
00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.100
Run it, and age disappears from the environment.

27
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.428
Then remove Black, the next value.

28
00:02:00.428 --> 00:02:01.780
It is gone too.

29
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:19.994
To remove many values at once, list them inside the brackets, separated by commas:

30
00:02:19.994 --> 00:02:22.820
City, demographic, Detail, location, and name.

31
00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.360
Run it, and the environment says: Environment is empty. A fresh start!

32
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:53.283
I add a line of hash signs, to separate this part of the script.

33
00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:57.120
Next, we will install the packages we need. Nice and tidy!

